cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use powerstamp in published work, please cite it."
title: "powerstamp: energy measurement that reports its own uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  powerstamp measures the energy consumed by a piece of work and reports the
  joule figure together with the sampling rate it actually achieved, the power
  rails and RAPL domains it actually covered, and a quantified measurement
  uncertainty. It refuses to emit a confident figure when the achieved sampling
  rate is too low for the duration of the run, and it never presents a model
  based estimate as a measurement.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
